// Phase 11.7.b R2b — keyed `<Child />` composition inside `{#for}`
// (`.fitzv` → WASM). The last "rendering core" slice of Phase 11.7:
// dynamic children with a stable identity + reconciliation, over a
// `List<primitive>` state field.
//
//   {#for name in columns}
//     <Column key="{name}" title="{name}" />
//   {/for}
//
// The `key="{...}"` attribute is NOT a prop — it gives each mounted
// child a stable identity. The WASM emitter keeps one instance PER
// key in a keyed cache (`HashMap<String, Rc<Column>>`), so a child —
// AND its local state — survives parent re-renders. Between renders a
// reconciliation sweep evicts any key that vanished from the list.
//
// WHY IT MATTERS (try it in the browser):
//   1. Click a column's "taps" button a few times — its own counter
//      goes up. Each `<Column />` holds its OWN `taps` state.
//   2. Click "re-render parent" — the parent's `bumps` changes, so
//      `App` re-renders and rebuilds the `{#for}` loop.
//   3. Every column's `taps` is STILL there. Because each key
//      (`"To Do"`, `"In Progress"`, `"Done"`) maps to the same cached
//      `Column` instance, its state is reused instead of reset.
//
// Contract of shape (R2b subset):
//   - `{#for x in <field>}` over `List<Int|Float|Str|Bool>` (11.7.b).
//   - `<Child key="{expr}" ... />` where `key` lowers to a primitive
//     — typically the loop variable. Interpolated props (`{expr}`)
//     into primitive child fields flow reactively (11.7.a).
//
// DEFERRED (clear pointers in the emitter): `{#for}` over a
// `List<nominal>` (e.g. `List<Card>`, needed by the kanban) waits on
// nominal-type support in the WASM target (Phase 11.7 R3 prereq);
// event bodies that push/remove list items (so keys appear/disappear
// at runtime and reconciliation is exercised live) are a separate
// 11.4.c debt — here the list is constant, so reconciliation runs but
// never evicts.

component App {
  state {
    columns: List<Str> = ["To Do", "In Progress", "Done"]
    bumps: Int = 0
  }

  event bump() { bumps = bumps + 1 }

  <template>
    <div class="board">
      <h1>Keyed children on WASM</h1>
      <p class="hint">Each column keeps its own tap counter. Tap a column, then re-render the parent — the counters survive because each key maps to a cached instance.</p>
      <button class="bump" @click="bump">re-render parent ({bumps})</button>
      <div class="columns">
        {#for name in columns}
          <Column key="{name}" title="{name}" />
        {/for}
      </div>
    </div>
  </template>

  <style scoped>
    .board { font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; }
    .hint { color: #666; font-size: 0.9em; }
    .bump { padding: 8px 16px; cursor: pointer; border: 1px solid #999; border-radius: 6px; background: white; margin-bottom: 16px; }
    .columns { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 12px; }
  </style>
}

component Column {
  state {
    title: Str = ""
    taps: Int = 0
  }

  event tap() { taps = taps + 1 }

  <template>
    <div class="column">
      <div class="title">{title}</div>
      <button class="tap" @click="tap">taps: {taps}</button>
    </div>
  </template>

  <style scoped>
    .column { flex: 1 1 140px; min-width: 120px; border: 1px solid #ddd; border-radius: 8px; padding: 16px; background: #fafafa; }
    .title { font-size: 0.85em; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em; color: #666; margin-bottom: 8px; }
    .tap { padding: 6px 12px; cursor: pointer; border: 1px solid #999; border-radius: 6px; background: white; }
  </style>
}
